message:
game: validation tab shows cost confidence, main uncertainty and like-for-like

From Max's hand-over (cost.py confidence on /validation rows):
- tooltip: 'Confidence 46% (medium, experimental) · data coverage 52%' and
  'Main uncertainty: <vendor model> (wide price range | weak price source |
  old price | bare vs equipped price unknown | similar model used as
  stand-in | configuration unknown)', names from /catalog;
- like_for_like false: greyed point with a dashed band, 'not like-for-like;
  left out of calibration' (reason shown when the backend gives one);
- split (when present): blind-test cases as diamonds and a 'Blind test: K of
  N inside the 80% band' headline, computed, never hard-coded;
- summary adds 'within ±25% of our P50: X of N'; a footnote computes the
  score's calibration on verified like-for-like cases (stated vs observed,
  'overconfident' when it is);
- table: sortable columns, 'Confidence (experimental)' as '46% medium' and a
  'Main uncertainty' column. ValidationRow gains the new optional fields.

